{
 "definition": "Z*_(q) = sum_{a mod q, gcd(a,q)=1} integral_T |R_{q,a}(beta)|^4 dbeta, R_{q,a} = F_N(a/q+beta) - (mu(q)/phi(q)) K_N(beta), computed exactly via DFT quadrature (frequency-exact, no sampling error beyond float64). This is the full-circle analogue of UPPER_BOUND.md Section 6's Z_(q), the same object RANK3_ROUTE_D.md Section 7 works with (no arc-transfer argument is available for the fourth moment, so the literal arc-restricted Z_(q) is not computed here, matching that document's own scope).",
